The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (tb[NFCTH_PRIV_DATA_LEN])
    return -EBUSY;
```
Reason:
This code immediately returns an `-EBUSY` error if the `NFCTH_PRIV_DATA_LEN` attribute is present, without checking whether the size of the private helper data actually differs from the existing size. This results in valid updates being incorrectly blocked even when the sizes are the same.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
size = ntohl(nla_get_be32(tb[NFCTH_PRIV_DATA_LEN]));
if (size != helper->data_len)
    return -EBUSY;
```
Reason:
These statements first retrieve the size of the private helper data from the attribute and then compare it to the existing size (`helper->data_len`). The `-EBUSY` error is only returned if the sizes differ, allowing valid updates to proceed when the sizes are the same, thus fixing the bug.

